No, there's no way of just bottling the water from a fountain or
sink--annoying, but I guess that's the way things are. Clear potions
pop up all over the place in potion shops and delicatessins, and if
they're uncursed they're really cheap--you can usually find some in
mine-town early on, and if the temple's co-aligned, well hey...

Also--if the items in question aren't things that could get erased,
it's possible (4/30 of the time) to uncurse something by dipping it in
a fountain. Then again, there's also a chance of something bad
happening if you do that, and of course spellbooks would get erased.

The nice thing about Valkyries (and I assume Barbarians--never used
Barbarians much)--you can load up on armor, dipping your long sword
into fountains once you're level 5 or more will eventually give you
Excalibur (only if you're lawful), and if you sacrifice enough you can
get Mjollnir early, which is really Mjollnir--two fairly easy and
powerful artifacts really early. Not to mention that, properly armored,
Valkyries are pretty much tanks, and whacking things with hammers and
swords doesn't run out of energy like Wizard's force bolt does.

And don't forget to #enhance your weapons skills when you get the
message "you feel more confident in your weapon skills". Since you
start out unskilled in war-hammers, this is particularly necessary for
Mjollnir, if and when you get it.

Also, I always get in trouble with wizards by panicking and casting
force bolt in a potion shop--suddenly, I have a level 3 character that
needs to kill a shopkeeper ;-).

